  "body": "## Dependency and review scope\n\nDraft, dependent on #363. Merge/review order remains #331 \u2192 #332 \u2192 #334 \u2192 #340 \u2192 #343 \u2192 #347 \u2192 #350 \u2192 #353 \u2192 #358 \u2192 #363 \u2192 this PR. Staging #344 remains a separate sibling after #343. Do not enable providers or merge this stack based on mock results.\n\nThis branch starts from updated payment core `e39abf5a4ce2151e03dbd91051ba508295081efb`, which already includes latest default `main` (`73edd77a36c8dcc73e5217303c62376ae684853b`, merged #333), and locally integrates #363 in `1d4acf7420ff532922a2c9623d1b854e3a76dbe6`. The large catalog/social/CI baseline diff is already-reviewed upstream ancestry, not newly authored functionality here. No remote PR was merged by this work. All 107 combined migration entries retain their source metadata; the one manifest-review fingerprint conflict was reviewed and resolved without bypassing the catalog gate.\n\nFor focused payment review, inspect **`1d4acf742..a902ca23a`** (seven code/test files), then the documentation commit:\n\n- `e0714bbbe`: runtime repair and database/adapter tests.\n- `9ca3c9086`: neutral PayPhone return/retry-key regression test.\n- `a902ca23a`: posted-ledger defense-in-depth regression test.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Map new authenticated PayPhone status-2 queries to cancellation/no-completed-charge. Official documentation inconsistently says canceled/rejected; the code does not infer issuer decline, buyer intent, a refund, or a void.\n- Lock and validate the original bound intent/attempt before applying no-charge evidence. Preserve coherent historical failed/canceled rows, timestamps, error labels and audit history.\n- Prevent repeated old no-charge observations from failing a newer processing checkout or rewriting a replacement payment that already succeeded.\n- Record the first authoritative cancellation consistently on intent and attempt while keeping an active order checkout retryable. Public API state remains `confirmed_no_charge`; no new wire enum or mobile/API generation change is needed.\n- Reject conflicting money, posted ledger or incoherent terminal history. Preserve operation conflict checks, caller-owned savepoint rollback, query-job fencing and provider budgets.\n\n## Verified local tests\n\nTest source: `a902ca23a4fa4e16fa2e7f9c7c766cf173ea9ffa`; subsequent changes are documentation. Full commands, dates, environments and limitations: [verification record](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/blob/4ccaaa190c4ae6b1d041d8eabd7eed8fd5327c5e/docs/payments/no-charge-replay-2026-09-15.md).\n\n- Stack `lts-24.42` / GHC 9.10.3: **2,592 examples, zero failures** (28.1933 s).\n- Real isolated PostgreSQL 16.10 harness with synthetic provider transport: **127 examples, zero failures** (9.4149 s), including concurrent replays, callback/worker paths, legacy history, replacement payments, financial conflicts, repeat migration, empty rollback/operator flag retention, and nonempty rollback refusal.\n- Focused web Jest: **13 tests in two suites passed**. Separate `npm run typecheck`: exit 0.\n- Integrated baseline release/catalog Node tests: **55 passed**.\n- Final catalog gate: **1,418 files / 1,126 candidates**, zero unreviewed/stale decisions; five local Markdown targets and `git diff --check` passed.\n\nThe initial Docker test run stalled alongside Docker API HTTP 500 responses and a timed-out test-port probe. Only this task's test child was terminated; that run failed/interrupted, not passed. The native Unix-socket rerun passed with no safety checks disabled; its private database is now stopped. Docker cleanup for the exact owned container `tdf-provider-retry-test-1485` remains unverified until Docker responds. No other project or Docker daemon was restarted. Inherited compiler/linker warnings remain visible.\n\n## Rollout and risks\n\nNo new migration or historical backfill for this repair. Retain the complete reviewed parent schema. Never bulk relabel old failed PayPhone payments. Drain old callback/scheduled consumers before an authorized rollout; rolling back to old binaries reintroduces replay mutations. Do not infer no charge from timeout, absent callback or an exhausted job. See [ADR 0121](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/blob/4ccaaa190c4ae6b1d041d8eabd7eed8fd5327c5e/docs/adr/0121-history-preserving-no-charge-reconciliation.md) and [operator runbooks](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/blob/4ccaaa190c4ae6b1d041d8eabd7eed8fd5327c5e/docs/payments/operator-runbooks.md).\n\nNo provider sandbox, staging payment, production deployment, live transaction, refund, void or payout was performed. No provider was enabled; no credentials were extracted or stored. No screenshots or mobile device/E2E results are claimed.\n\nExisting staging health URLs returned HTTP 200, but the metadata-only inspector could not authenticate hosting, establish a source SHA, or qualify a provider. Approved app-scoped Fly access (`FLY_STAGING_API_TOKEN` / `FLY_STAGING_WEB_TOKEN`, or authorized local login), genuine merchant sandbox/contract/method evidence, webhook registration and legal/accounting/PCI review remain required. Unknown-resource recovery, late-paid fulfillment, remaining adapters/business flows and compliant marketplace payouts remain separate unfinished work. This is not completion of the overall payment platform.\n",
